# OpenAgent — TODO

Check off only work covered by tests or a documented manual verification.

## v0.2.0 — Browser Manager
- [x] Separate a browser manager from service/model adapters.
- [x] Support dedicated persistent profiles and local CDP attachment.
- [x] Enforce tab ownership, page limits, and per-adapter navigation origins.
- [x] Represent startup, stopped, connected, failed, and disconnected states.
- [x] Handle navigation failure without leaving a managed tab open.
- [x] Require explicit transport restart after disconnection; do not replay requests.
- [x] Make Playwright optional and mock-test the browser lifecycle.
- [x] Use Windows-friendly default port 12321 and reserved-port fallback.
- [x] Document Windows setup and browser probes.
- [ ] Run `browser probe` in headed and CDP modes on user's Windows machine.
- [ ] Confirm Python 3.10 install and v0.2 full test suite on Windows.

## v0.3 — First authorized model adapter
- [ ] Define a typed browser provider contract and error codes.
- [ ] Implement fixture-based chat response completion/cancellation detection.
- [ ] Implement provider capability discovery (model, effort, projects, files).
- [ ] Define first-provider permission and terms review before live integration.
- [ ] Add prompt/response transfer preserving context and request IDs.
- [ ] Add native tool-call translation for OpenCode compatibility.
- [ ] Add fixture tests for upload/download, checksums and safe paths.

## Later — client interoperability and agent runtime
- [ ] Test OpenCode + 9Router routes and streaming against real adapters.
- [ ] Add `/v1/responses` and provider-native streaming where available.
- [ ] Build checkpointing across browser conversations without duplicating commands.
- [ ] Implement workspace/shell/file tools in a **separate standalone agent**.
- [ ] Add Git checkpoints, approvals, steering, and patch rollback.

## Guardrails
- Never run model-produced shell commands in the bridge.
- Do not treat reconnect as permission to resubmit an ambiguous remote turn.
- Never commit profile/cookie/session/token material.
- Do not claim support for a web model until a real test proves it.
